a GET, a HEAD, a POST gathered whole, a POST in pieces, a 404:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  HEADERS 1 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=18
  DATA 1 18 'hello example.test' END_STREAM
  HEADERS 3 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=18 END_STREAM
  HEADERS 5 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=8
  DATA 5 8 'whole 11' END_STREAM
  HEADERS 7 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=11
  DATA 7 11 'pieces 9000' END_STREAM
  HEADERS 9 :status=404 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=0 END_STREAM
  HEADERS 11 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=8
  DATA 11 8 'a=1; b=2' END_STREAM
a response in pieces, through MORE:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  HEADERS 1 :status=200 server=goose
  DATA 1 6 'first '
  DATA 1 5 'more '
  DATA 1 5 'more '
  DATA 1 0 '' END_STREAM
a response's fields lowercased, HTTP/1.1's connection fields dropped, and a head held open:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  HEADERS 1 :status=200 server=goose x-mixed-case=1 upgrades=kept content-location=/kept content-length=2
  DATA 1 2 'ok' END_STREAM
  HEADERS 5 :status=200 server=goose x-f0=v x-f1=v x-f2=v x-f3=v x-f4=v x-f5=v x-f6=v x-f7=v x-f8=v x-f9=v x-f10=v x-f11=v x-f12=v x-f13=v x-f14=v x-f15=v x-f16=v x-f17=v x-f18=v x-f19=v x-f20=v x-f21=v x-f22=v x-f23=v x-f24=v x-f25=v x-f26=v x-f27=v x-f28=v x-f29=v x-f30=v x-f31=v x-f32=v x-f33=v content-length=4
  DATA 5 4 'long' END_STREAM
  HEADERS 3 :status=200 server=goose x-held=yes
  DATA 3 5 'more '
  DATA 3 5 'more '
  DATA 3 0 '' END_STREAM
a stream window of 10, then WINDOW_UPDATEs:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  HEADERS 1 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=100
  DATA 1 10 'abcdefghij'
  DATA 1 30 'klmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefgh'
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  DATA 1 40 'opqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijkl'
  DATA 1 20 'cdefghijklmnopqrstuv' END_STREAM
padded bodies at a server stream window of 100:
  SETTINGS 0 5 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 3 +80
  HEADERS 1 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=8
  DATA 1 8 'whole 30' END_STREAM
  HEADERS 3 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=9
  DATA 3 9 'pieces 60' END_STREAM
a stream that waits holds back no other:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  HEADERS 3 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=18
  DATA 3 18 'hello example.test' END_STREAM
  (handler: TIMEOUT)
  HEADERS 1 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=6
  DATA 1 6 'waited' END_STREAM
streams that wait at once, each live until it ends:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  live: true and true
  (handler: WAKE)
  HEADERS 1 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=6
  DATA 1 6 'waited' END_STREAM
  then sends to streams 1 and 3: STALE, SENT
  (handler: WAKE)
  HEADERS 3 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=6
  DATA 3 6 'waited' END_STREAM
  then sends to streams 1 and 3: STALE, STALE
upgrade, malformed requests, and too many streams:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  HEADERS 1 :status=501 server=goose content-length=0 END_STREAM
  RST_STREAM 3 PROTOCOL_ERROR
  RST_STREAM 5 PROTOCOL_ERROR
  RST_STREAM 7 PROTOCOL_ERROR
  RST_STREAM 9 PROTOCOL_ERROR
  RST_STREAM 15 REFUSED_STREAM
  GOAWAY 0 PROTOCOL_ERROR last 15
trailers past max_head, and a :path and a :method HTTP/1.1 refuses:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  RST_STREAM 1 PROTOCOL_ERROR
  RST_STREAM 3 PROTOCOL_ERROR
  RST_STREAM 5 PROTOCOL_ERROR
  RST_STREAM 7 PROTOCOL_ERROR
  HEADERS 9 :status=404 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=0 END_STREAM
100-continue, another expectation, and a handler that ends keep-alive:
  SETTINGS 0 4 values
  WINDOW_UPDATE 0 +983041
  SETTINGS 0 ACK 0 values
  HEADERS 1 :status=100
  HEADERS 3 :status=417 server=goose content-length=0 END_STREAM
  RST_STREAM 3 NO_ERROR
  HEADERS 1 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=7
  DATA 1 7 'whole 4' END_STREAM
  HEADERS 5 :status=200 server=goose content-type=text/plain content-length=3
  DATA 5 3 'bye' END_STREAM
  GOAWAY 0 NO_ERROR last 5
